  "definition": "BuChE stands for butyrylcholinesterase, an enzyme involved in cholinesterase activity that is discussed as a key therapeutic target in Alzheimer’s disease research. In the source, it is measured because some compounds can inhibit BuChE, which may be relevant to efforts to address progressive cognitive decline.",
